Z||000009||AkursedX||03-24-2001||09:55 PM||||How depressing   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Seeing all these wonderful Fieros together under a beautiful, warm, sunlit sky, and me and my '88GT are stuck here in freezing cold Buffalo!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>At least I got to work on my car for a little today, although it was 28 degrees out.  Thank god for a garage!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I liked all of the cars in the pictures, except for that black one with the "Weapon R" sticker and that huge fin, giant fog lamps, and those 2 plastic tubes sticking up from the engine vents.  Thumbs down on that.  A little too tacky for me.  And could someone tell me what a "Weapon R" is.  And does the sticker give any added hp gains??    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> But I do like the flushmount headlights.<BR>But who am I to judge, to each his/her own<p>[This message has been edited by AkursedX (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000010||Shaft||03-24-2001||10:15 PM||||Weapon R is a brand of intake.||||reg||1
Z||000011||AkursedX||03-24-2001||10:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaft:<BR><B>Weapon R is a brand of intake.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh it is?  Thank you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I feel dumb.<P>So does Weapon R really make intakes for a Fiero?  Or is it a modified piece?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Slammed Fiero||03-24-2001||10:29 PM||||Weapon R is Honda stuff..headers , intakes....long grain , minute , seasoned...your typical rice<P>JN||||reg||1
Z||000013||Spyder||03-24-2001||10:38 PM||||Today it was Sunny, 84 degrees, and Absolutely Gorgeous Day. <BR>I had a great time today, finally got to put some faces with screen names.<P>I tried to get pics of the unusual things that we don’t see on the stock Fiero.<P>On the convertible I only got one pic with the digital camera, I think I took some pics of it with the regular 35mm camera, I’ll see in a couple of days.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||03-24-2001||10:59 PM||||OH My GOD!!<P>That black thing won it's class!!!! the car with the big ass fog lights (black one with weapon R decal)!! I just talked to Lisa she said it won first in her class!!<P>POLITICS!!! Could it have to do with the Flordia Plates on the car..<P>sad sad day<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000015||Eric||03-24-2001||11:20 PM||||Those are headlights for foglights.  And I wear hats for shoes.<P>Truthfully, I don't like any of those cars too much, except for Phil's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I can appreciate all the work that went into a lot of that stuff especially the intake that was polished; that was incredible.  But the rest of it looks tacky.  I hope there were some clean stock type cars their too.  Can we have some pics of those?||||reg||1
Z||000016||sluppy123||03-24-2001||11:27 PM||||Anybody happen to know who owns the Silver fastback with the helmet sitting on top of it? Or know what kind of wheels it has? I love those wheels!!!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered, Nitrous<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=7653930&p=37756786&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||10
Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||03-24-2001||11:28 PM||||Actually the second car from the top is Chris moores Northstar powered Convertible... Very very nice clean car.. not even a decal that says N*.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000018||fyerstarter||03-24-2001||11:39 PM||||Sluppy:  Those are actually a pretty common wheel style. Check out <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A>  and there are probably several manufacturers that carry a style similar to that. One that comes to mind is MB Motoring, they are very inexpensive and I thin they have some like that. ||||reg||1
Z||000019||FieroJoe||03-24-2001||11:45 PM||||I like chromed intake plenum, but I dont know about the mirror, it seems kinda low-riderish to me.<P>Some sweet paintjobs there, especially that reddish one (2nd pic down)<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||sqoach||03-25-2001||01:21 AM||||i love the chromed v6. that is sweet! i also like the one above it with the flames. looks pretty neat. some of those fieros are pretty scary though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>hopefully i'll be able to make it to a "big" show sometime before i turn 50  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||10
Z||000021||Pontiaddict||03-25-2001||01:44 AM||||I like the black and white fastback in the first pic. I might use a different scheme on my car eventually.<BR>I also like the roof scoop on the green car, though it would be better if somehow made functional. The rest of the car shows alot of work, but it was too much for my taste.<BR>The grey Notchback looks like a racecar without being ricey, though the formula logos have to go.<BR>Phil's Formula is cool too.<BR>That black fastback needs to be cleaned up, ALOT! Loose the fake vents on the hood, the scoops and wing in the back, and the decals on the front. The head.. er, foglights look weird enough to stay. I wouldn't have given it an award though.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 03-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||bHooper||03-25-2001||08:52 AM||||I didn't recognize Chris's N* convertible.  We got to see/hear it, last wednesday night.  The paint looks much different in the daylight, without rain!<P>Fella's, Fella's, Fella's, let me tell you... that is one <B><I>Sweeeeeet</B></I> sounding car!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000023||MrPBody||03-25-2001||10:29 AM||||I vote for the silver Formula with triple hood vents!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Yellow88GT||03-25-2001||10:50 AM||||Any more info on the convertible GT?<P>PLEASE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jerry||||reg||1
Z||000025||Tina||03-25-2001||11:39 AM||||Ahhh, could it be true.<BR>It has been done?! You guys and girls soaking<BR>up the sun down there, could somebody check<BR>the Gaslid/cover(silver) on the black Fiero.<BR>Please,(ehh) I mean pretty please. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Is it really the AUDI TT COVER!<P>Tina,<BR>heat cranked on high in the garage.<P>Anyways,enjoy guys and girls, hope you have a blast  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000026||firstfiero||03-25-2001||12:01 PM||||    Everything looks SWEET except that riced out fiero. Think I'll go out today and get some black tubing to come out of mine....looks chincy! oh well....Still killing me not to be their....<P>------------------<BR>'86 fiero Se<BR>    Todd<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!!||||reg||14
Z||000027||Spyder||03-25-2001||12:56 PM||||Here is a link to the kit cars that were there: <A HREF="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/Daytona2001.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.markalexandermiller.com/Daytona2001.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||TwisT||03-25-2001||02:13 PM||||Hmmm...<P>Well,  obviously I wish I was there instead of being stuck in crappy-cold South Dakota!  Thanks for sharing those pictures with the forum.  <P>I'm not sure what to think about some of these cars.  I try to keep my opinion at bay on this forum because I understand that everyone has different tastes.  But some of the mods on these cars look absolutely HIDEOUS!  OMG!!!  I can't help but think that illegal substances are in abundance around Daytona!<P>That said,  there's some really nice one's too.  Again,  thanks for sharing witht the forum!<P>Brett<P>  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000029||AkursedX||03-25-2001||04:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>OH My GOD!!<P>That black thing won it's class!!!! the car with the big ass fog lights (black one with weapon R decal)!! I just talked to Lisa she said it won first in her class!!<P>POLITICS!!! Could it have to do with the Flordia Plates on the car..<P>sad sad day<P>JM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Wow, that is REALLY sad.  What class was it in??  Do they have some sort of class for the tackiest most non-functional mods??  <P><BR>||||reg||9
Z||000030||87GT||03-25-2001||04:42 PM||||If you look at the picture posted at 9:30, you can see the the back right rear of my car.  Its at the extreme right of the picture.  The black fiero in the picture with all the stuff on it is from Orlando.  He was sure proud of his car.  The show was great, couldnt have asked for better weather.  The judges said my hood was tight.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">    I had fun anyways.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000031||87GT||03-25-2001||06:11 PM||||Im pretty sure that the black car with the huge fog lights was in the SCMC class, if it was, it did not win.  I never saw the owner go up and get any kind of award.||||reg||1
Z||000032||Alex4mula||03-25-2001||08:45 PM||||The silver GT with the helmet on top is from a girl from our West Palm Beach club. Those wheels are discontinued model. You can find similar but not the same. I like them very much but like my new ones more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000033||Black88GT||03-25-2001||09:14 PM||||It's a sad day in the world of Fiero's.  Did anyone else notice the excessive rice pictured?  OMG, its a disgrace.  More nonfunctional hood scoops then a Subaru.  Raised wings galore and FOR GOD SAKES A WEAPON R STICKER?!?!  Yellow stickers and a cowl induction hood?.  I bet they all have stock 2.8's or even worse, 4 bangers.  What does that black Fiero have over his decklid vents, HVAC hoses from Home Depot or something?<P>If this is the way Fiero's are going (ala RICE) then I think I am going to jump ship while there's still some decency left.  This is pathetic.  I am sure there were some non-rice Fiero's there.  Please tell me there were some non-rice Fiero's there (other then Phils 3800SC and a few others pictured).  Please.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000034||87GT||03-25-2001||09:38 PM||||Most of the pictures above are of the wildest looking fieros there.  There were a lot of beautiful stock and slight modified fieros.  The best of show award went to a 87GT All stock in the original blue paint.  The black fiero with the Type R stuff on it has the 2.8 in it still.  He and I talked quite a bit since we were parked next to each other.   ||||reg||1
Z||000035||LZeitgeist||03-25-2001||09:49 PM||||Hey, that yellow Formula with the black taillight panel and the raised with belongs to our very own Phil!! <P>Hey, Phil - gonna be back in Virginia this year?||||reg||1
Z||000036||Hank is Here||03-25-2001||09:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Actually the second car from the top is Chris moores Northstar powered Convertible... Very very nice clean car.. not even a decal that says N*.<BR>JM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>All I can say is that I love to color of that car.  Looks sort of like the stock color but isn't||||reg||1
Z||000037||Shaft||03-26-2001||01:11 AM||||That silver GT with the helmet on it belongs to a girl!!!!! WOW! I'M IN LOVE! Get her on the forum so we can have another girl on here.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
