Z||000039||RobertVol||03-26-2001||02:07 AM||||As that Northstar was leaving the guy goosed it a few times and all I can say is....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>That was one of sweetest sounding cars there! <P><p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000040||Slammed Fiero||03-26-2001||10:45 AM||||Chris Moore Bought the convert as a 6cyl auto , with that paint job. He converted the car over to a Northstar in a matter of weeks , and just finally got the car sorted out last week. As for the color we will have to ask him , he is lurking around on the forum somewhere , I know he is driving back to indianna today from NC. You can email him @ northstar87@excite.com<P><BR>I have yet to ride in the convert , but from what I hear it is verrrry loud. I have ridden in his 87 GT N* ...such smoooth progressive power..yummy<P><BR>JM||||reg||1
Z||000041||sdm1964||03-26-2001||02:33 PM||||Hope you guys had fun. Looks like more cars than last year. Anyone have any numbers of cars? I was thinking about yall, all weekend. I hope robert did not forget my t-shirt. I am primed and ready for next year. I have come to one conclusion, There are NO fieros in bosnia.||||reg||14
Z||000042||Tigger||03-26-2001||04:10 PM||||Pretty cool, wish I was there.  Looks like there was lots to see.<P>Did they let you guys take a pace lap around the track with your Fieros?  That would be cool...||||reg||1
Z||000043||Ronnie||03-26-2001||07:01 PM||||Hey Spyder, You didn't show everybody the Lincoln Continental kit car!!! HeHe!<BR>Couldn't believe my eyes, to think someone would do that to a Fiero!!||||reg||6
Z||000044||The Beauty||03-26-2001||08:13 PM||||Sluppy123-<P>I was at the show and talked with the girl.  She's a member of the West Palm Fiero club in Florida.  I didn't get her name but she is a big fiero buff.  She brought three of her fieros to the show and I think that the silver one placed.  I think anybody from that club could tell you her name and help you out.<P>    The Beauty<BR>    South Florida Fiero Enthusiast  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||4
Z||000045||87GT||03-26-2001||08:21 PM||||A spoke to a judge that did one of the womans 3 Fieros and he said one of them didnt place because she had seat covers and a cover on her steering wheel.  The car was immaculate but lost because of that.  He said that means the owner could be hiding defects on the interior.  ||||reg||1
Z||000046||FieroLisa||03-26-2001||08:48 PM||||I just got home...aughh sooooo tired. Driving all day yesterday and today.  Weather was beautiful, but I was sick all weekend so I spent my time either cleaning the car or ready to pass out. So to anyone that I met, if I wasn't my usual peppy self, sorry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>But it was a great time, Chris and I took a ton of pics, they will be on my website within the next week or so.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT- 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air,<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000047||Alex4mula||03-26-2001||10:45 PM||||The name of the girl from the WPB club is Brygida. She had 3 GTs in the show. A white one with chrome wheels, a red one and the silver. The red got 4th place in her class. That one had won abot 5 times before. She spent most of the time preparing the silver for no prize. Sad because to me that's one of the coolest GTs I have seen. I do agree that if you have seat covers, etc you will be deducted points cause seems like hiding. Anyway the silver has very nice Mr. Mike seats. She realy loves Fieros. Very nice person too.||||reg||1
Z||000048||RobertVol||03-26-2001||10:54 PM||||SDM e mail me !! <P>I got your shirt for ya  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000049||Philphine||03-27-2001||12:19 AM||||so thats what compleated projects look like.||||reg||1
Z||000050||Cheever2||03-27-2001||12:40 AM||||So what was Saturday like?  What did you do all day - look at cars and talk to the other owners?  Anybody find a particularly great place to eat?<P>Also, do they MAKE you go away while they're judging your car?<P>I know you guys are still tired from the trip home, but basically I just want to know all about it, you know, for next year.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000051||87GT||03-27-2001||09:07 AM||||It was kind of up to the owner if they wanted to hang around while their car was being judged.  I didnt really want to hang around because I knew my car still wasnt show car worthy and I didnt want to hear them pick it apart.  While the judging was going on, I was going around looking at the other fieros and talking to owners.  When I wasnt doing that, I was checking out all the classic cars that were there.  Huge show, couldnt see everything in one day.  ||||reg||1
Z||000052||Ralfy9862||03-27-2001||10:19 AM||||what do those stickers say that some cars have on the lower quarters and there is also some on the fenders? Where <BR>Can you buy them anywheres<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000053||FieroLisa||03-27-2001||01:05 PM||||Cheever - I always hang around my car for judging. If they want to open a door or see something, I want to be there to do it.||||reg||1
Z||000054||northstar87||03-27-2001||01:51 PM||||Thanks for all of the nice compliments.  Lisa and I made it home last night with no problems.  It was a great time.  The color of the car is Candy Wild Cherry.  It is from the House of Color.  I hope that helps.  I will talk more later.<P>Chris Moore<BR>ASE Master Auto Tech and Auto Instructor||||reg||1
Z||000055||Frank Martin||03-28-2001||10:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>OH My GOD!!<P>That black thing won it's class!!!! the car with the big ass fog lights (black one with weapon R decal)!! I just talked to Lisa she said it won first in her class!!<P>I THINK THAT YOU AND LISA ARE WRONG.  IF YOU LOOK AT THE WINNERS LIST ON THE DAYTONA SHOW SITE YOU WILL FIND THAT THE WINNER OF STREET CUSTOM GT WAS WILLAIM HOUSE OF OHIO.  THE CR YOU ARE TALKING ABUT DID NOT TAKE A TROPHY.  <BR>CHECK THE LIST AT:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/daytona2001/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/daytona2001/</A> <P>AS A MATTER OF FACT THERE WERE A LOT OF OUT OF STATE CARS THAT DID VERY WELL.  ASK CHRIS MOORE<P>LATER   <BR>HAVE A GOOD EVEING<P><BR>POLITICS!!! Could it have to do with the Flordia Plates on the car..<P>sad sad day<P>JM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000056||wwh0001||04-02-2001||03:11 PM||||<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR>OH My GOD!!<BR>That black thing won it's class!!!! the car with the big ass fog lights (black one with weapon R decal)!! I just talked to Lisa she said it won first in her class!!<P>I THINK THAT YOU AND LISA ARE WRONG. IF YOU LOOK AT THE WINNERS LIST ON THE DAYTONA SHOW SITE YOU WILL FIND THAT THE WINNER OF STREET CUSTOM GT WAS WILLAIM HOUSE OF OHIO. THE CR YOU ARE TALKING ABUT DID NOT TAKE A TROPHY. <BR>CHECK THE LIST AT: <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/daytona2001/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/daytona2001/</A>  <P>AS A MATTER OF FACT THERE WERE A LOT OF OUT OF STATE CARS THAT DID VERY WELL. ASK CHRIS MOORE<P>LATER <BR>HAVE A GOOD EVEING<P><BR>POLITICS!!! Could it have to do with the Flordia Plates on the car..<P><BR>  HI there. The car you are talking about is mine that won First Place in street custom gt. It is black with rainbow stipes with a modern version of the pegasus ( 12 layered stiping on the hood and deck lid) It was one of the last ones judged that day and was in the last row. ||||reg||1
