Z||000059||Fierodave2001||04-04-2001||12:56 PM||||Hi,  Dave here,<P>I own the blue stock 87 GT that won the best Stock Paint, Best of Stock Group, and Best of Show.  It has only 1730 miles !<BR> Can be seen at follow sites :<BR> <A HREF="http://www.sunline.net/showroom/dave" TARGET=_blank>www.sunline.net/showroom/dave</A> <P>Other Daytona pics can be seen in this site:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.zing.com/album/?id=4292795563&code=1494566&mode=invite" TARGET=_blank>http://www.zing.com/album/?id=4292795563&code=1494566&mode=invite</A> <P><BR>I still can not believe it.  There were so many really sharp cars in the show.  I'm just so proud to have my car selected.<P>Hello to all those that I met at the show.<BR>I've owned the car since Sept 86, when I ordered it.  I earlier owned a 84 4cyl, then traded for an 85v6.  Just loved the heck out of each.  When I bought the 87, I knew with the first look, it was a keeper.<P><BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GT:<BR><B>Most of the pictures above are of the wildest looking fieros there.  There were a lot of beautiful stock and slight modified fieros.  The best of show award went to a 87GT All stock in the original blue paint.  The black fiero with the Type R stuff on it has the 2.8 in it still.  He and I talked quite a bit since we were parked next to each other.   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by Fierodave2001 (edited 04-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000060||Brygida Fieros||04-11-2001||04:30 PM||||To everyone whom posted here in regards to my silver GT:<P>Pictures 8, 10 and 20 from the top feature my GTs (silver, red and white one). To those who wanted to know if I got a trophy?... no... I received 4th Place plaque with my red GT in Street Custom GT class. Last year in Daytona I took 1st place in Street Custom and 2nd Place in Custom class with my red & white GTs. But this year the competition was so tough. And of course congrats to all of you that competed. <BR>As to the rims on my silver GT, they're about 7-8 years old, 17' Elysses, made in France. (Discontinued and no longer available).<BR>If anyone wishes to look at any more Daytona pictures... check out my album on zing.com <A HREF="http://www.zing.com/album/pictures.html?id=4292837505" TARGET=_blank>http://www.zing.com/album/pictures.html?id=4292837505</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Brygida T.<BR>Palm Beach Fieros<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/fl3/palmbeachfieros||||reg||1
